so i need  50 grams  of cocoa powder  [Music]  and you can see  just how lumpy  that cocoa powder is and so i just  because i have it in the sieve  i can just  get all those lumps out and it's all  smooth so now all of my ingredients are  weighed out i've only dirtied one bowl  because that's the kind of recipe this  is it's a one bowl just dump it all in  and stir and that's it  if you don't have a scale  and you have to use measuring cups it's  okay you can do it i highly recommend  that you get a scale especially if you  like to bake a lot  but  there are different ways to measure  flour and so it's always a great idea to  go to the front of a cookbook and see  how the author does it does the author  [Music]  spoon and sweep which means that you  would spoon  the  flower right into the measuring cup just  like this  and so it's aerating the flour a little  bit you're gonna get a little bit less  flour this way so you're aerating the  flour  into the measuring cup and then  you just take a knife or a spatula and  sweep it  flat like that or does the author want  you to scoop and sweep which means that  you dip  the cup down into the flour and then  sweep it off  those two things  are going to get you a very different  amount of flour so it's really handy to  know how the author wrote the recipe the  scale takes all of the guesswork out so  get yourself a scale  make your baking easier make it more  consistent it's one of my absolute  favorite kitchen tools so if you get a  scale if you use this kitchen hack  please tag me at zoe bakes and use  hashtag  drewberrymoreshow on all social media so  that we can see what you're up to  and you can go to  thedrewberrymoreshow.com and get more  kitchen hacks and recipes and enjoy your  baking  [Music]  you
 

